Lets the simulated host's commit guard pass a file whose kind, size and
mtime match what the engine expected, whatever its exec bit, as before
d12fec3 (§7.5 step 6), so a chmod between a losing version's record and the
commit that displaces its file goes through. Only that fix's exec
comparison is undone: the guard still compares a symlink's target, SetMeta
is still guarded, and the scan fast path is unchanged.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_chmod_under_a_pending_commit_is_changed_underneath
test: delocal-sim sim::tests::the_commit_guard_refuses_a_file_whose_exec_bit_changed

diff --git a/crates/sim/src/sim.rs b/crates/sim/src/sim.rs
index 4e18586..f8da56f 100644
--- a/crates/sim/src/sim.rs
+++ b/crates/sim/src/sim.rs
@@ -2731,7 +2731,10 @@ fn rel(s: &str) -> RelPath {
 fn expected_matches(file: Option<&File>, expected: Option<&Observed>) -> bool {
     match (file, expected) {
         (None, None) => true,
-        (Some(f), Some(e)) => e.unchanged_by_stat(&f.observed()),
+        (Some(f), Some(e)) => e.unchanged_by_stat(&Observed {
+            exec: e.exec,
+            ..f.observed()
+        }),
         _ => false,
     }
 }
